    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1031">

                <pb facs="0957" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/1100</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Assistant Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peters</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-03">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Referring to your letter of to-day’s date<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1031-f1"/> and to
                    my conference with Mr. Hamilton, the collector at Norfolk,
                    Department will raise no objection to clearance of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gladstone</hi> If Appropriate Parties Give Assurance Under Oath That The
                    Cargo Will Be Discharged At The Foreign Port Or Ports To Which It Is Consigned.
                    See Department’S Telegram November 24.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1031-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
